crypt32: Don't close the root-store file descriptors twice.

import_certs_from_file() wraps the caller's fd in fdopen() and fclose()s the
FILE, which closes fd. Its caller import_certs_from_path() then calls
close(fd) on the same number. If another thread opens a file in between and
gets that number, the second close() closes the other thread's descriptor.
On Android, bionic's fdsan aborts the process when that descriptor belongs
to a FILE* ("attempted to close file descriptor N, expected to be unowned,
actually owned by FILE*"). The root store is synced on the first ROOT store
open in a process (for WoW: the first TLS check at Log In), while bionic's
getaddrinfo() makes a FILE* on every lookup, so WoW died at Log In.

Fix: read through a dup() of fd, so fclose() closes only the duplicate and
the caller's close(fd) is the only close of fd.

Upstream Wine master (checked 2026-09-24) still has the same code in
dlls/crypt32/unixlib.c (fdopen/fclose in import_certs_from_file, close(fd)
in import_certs_from_path); not fixed upstream.

Applies to proton-wine 4f1adc72 (the tree the proton-10.0-1-arm64ec-wow
package was built from).

diff --git a/dlls/crypt32/unixlib.c b/dlls/crypt32/unixlib.c
index 5e65302ac9a..543c233c7fd 100644
--- a/dlls/crypt32/unixlib.c
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/unixlib.c
@@ -498,16 +498,25 @@ static BOOL base64_to_cert( const char *str )
     return TRUE;
 }
 
-/* Reads the file fd, and imports any certificates in it into store. */
+/* Reads the file fd, and imports any certificates in it into store.
+ * The caller owns fd and closes it, so read through a dup(): fclose() on a FILE
+ * made from fd itself closes fd here, the caller then closes the same number
+ * again, and that second close can hit a descriptor another thread has opened
+ * in the meantime (bionic's fdsan aborts the process on it). */
 static void import_certs_from_file( int fd )
 {
-    FILE *fp = fdopen(fd, "r");
+    int fd2 = dup(fd);
+    FILE *fp = fd2 == -1 ? NULL : fdopen(fd2, "r");
     char line[1024];
     BOOL in_cert = FALSE;
     struct DynamicBuffer saved_cert = { 0, 0, NULL };
     int num_certs = 0;
 
-    if (!fp) return;
+    if (!fp)
+    {
+        if (fd2 != -1) close(fd2);
+        return;
+    }
     TRACE("\n");
     while (fgets(line, sizeof(line), fp))
     {
